# Cloudflare Pages routing for the shop's dynamic product URLs.
# This is a 200 rewrite (serve this content, keep the original URL in the
# browser's address bar) rather than a redirect.
#
# Two Cloudflare Pages behaviors that make this rule less obvious than it
# looks, both confirmed with `wrangler pages dev`:
#  1. A rewrite never exposes its destination's query string to client-side
#     JS — location.search stays whatever it was on the original request.
#     So product.js reads the slug from location.pathname instead, which a
#     rewrite correctly leaves as the original /product/:slug.
#  2. Cloudflare Pages unconditionally 308-redirects ANY resolved .html
#     path to its extensionless form — including internal rewrite
#     destinations, not just direct requests. Targeting /product.html here
#     (even with no query string) triggers that redirect, which collapses
#     the path to a bare /product with the slug lost entirely. Targeting
#     the already-extensionless /product avoids it.
#
# Not understood by `npx serve` locally — use /product?slug=... directly,
# or `npx wrangler pages dev .` which does understand this file
# (see docs/SHOP_SETUP.md).
/product/:slug  /product  200
